media: i2c: add the liuqin IMX596/SC202CS sensor driver

One driver for the two auxiliary modules (front IMX596 on csiphy2, depth
SC202CS on csiphy1), with its DT binding and the Kconfig/Makefile entries,
including the findings from bring-up:

- the IMX596 streams with the 16-bit write 0x0100 = 0x0103 (the byte write
  never actually started it);
- chip-id retries with a reset pulse between attempts: the module I2C comes
  up marginal and one failed probe leaves the whole async notifier incomplete
  (every camera disappears);
- measured link rates: 678.4 MHz front, 360 MHz depth (the old values were
  off by ~60% / 2x and left the PHY mistuned);
- the depth link is a single lane;
- the IMX596 analogue gain takes the vendor's Sony-style code, and the depth
  sensor's 20-bit exposure layout is handled;
- subdevices are named after their model so the per-sensor tuning files load.

The register/mode tables are machine-generated from the MIUI sensor-module
containers (the generator lived in the bring-up branch).  Both modules capture
through the shared csid0/vfe0_rdi0 modelled in 0022.

